        "value": "Time went by fast. His children had grown up and moved out, and his wife had passed away. The old man continued to fish, but now fishing only meant a connection with the past."
       },
       {
        "type": "markdown",
        "value": "After sunset, the old man picked up his fishing rod and walked down to the river bank. He cast his line into the water, waiting for a bite. Suddenly, his line moved, and he pulled in the line with great excitement. It was a big fish! In the past, he would have been proud of catching such a fish. But now, it was just a reminder of the passing of time. He let out a deep breath and decided to set the fish free."
       },
